  "id": "COMPOUND:31899 - PROTEIN:5783",
  "verbalization": "Nortoxiferine, dihydro- is implicated in the pathway leading to M19-MEL through multiple targets, all of which are components of the proteasome system. The evidence suggests that Nortoxiferine, dihydro- acts as a target for several compounds, including 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, and 5-Oxobrucine. These targets are all involved in the proteasome's regulatory functions, which are critical for cellular protein degradation and homeostasis. The presence of multiple targets indicates that Nortoxiferine, dihydro- may exert its effects through a complex network of interactions, potentially modulating proteasome activity to influence M19-MEL. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of the proteasome in mediating the biological effects of Nortoxiferine, dihydro-, suggesting a possible mechanism by which the compound interacts with cellular processes to affect M19-MEL.",
